# Accepted-paper sample (NeurIPS 2023–2024 main track)

Purpose: ground the budget in `VENUE.md` §6–§7 in what accepted work close to this study looks like.

**Selection.** I listed the NeurIPS 2023 and 2024 proceedings indexes (`https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/<year>`), filtered titles by keywords (ranking, Elo, Bradley, LLM-as-judge, evaluation, influence, data removal, preference) and chose 13 main-track papers on evaluation methodology, pairwise ranking, LLM-judge or preference evaluation, and influence or data-removal analysis. Datasets-and-Benchmarks track papers were left out (different track). The choice is mine, by title, not random, and not exhaustive. Only 2023–2024 papers were taken, so none can cite the paper the objective forbids; none of them is that paper.

**Measurement.** `accepted_sample/scripts/analyze.py` (pages, captions before the first "References" heading), `links.py` (distinct `cite.*` hyperref links before and after the reference heading), `struct.py` (abstract and introduction word counts, headings, first-figure page). They read PDFs in a directory outside this repository (`/hutian/venue_data/pdfs`, downloaded from the proceedings; not committed). Results: `accepted_sample/sample.csv`. Figure and table counts are captioned items in the main text (a multi-panel figure is one). Spot check of caption lists against six PDFs: no disagreement. Word counts include text extracted from figures for the main-text length; abstract and introduction counts come from regex-delimited text and are accurate to a few percent. `main_text_pages_camera_ready` is 10 for those whose reference list starts at the top of page 11, and "9-10" where it starts partway down page 10 or 11 after a few lines.

**Caveat.** These are camera-ready versions (10 content pages in 2023 and 2024), whereas the submission for 2026 is 9 pages.

